# Geometry optimization of LiH on a NEMO reference: `--optimize --wf=nemo`.
#
# Same deck as scf_lih_optimize, run with a different `--wf` -- the optimizer, the
# thresholds and the starting geometry are identical, so the pair is a cross-check
# between the two engines: a regularized (nuclear-cusp-free) reference and a plain
# SCF one must find the same minimum. They do, to ~1e-4 bohr at these thresholds
# (3.033905 vs 3.034046 bohr), and each case pins its own value.
#
# nemo also needs the wavefunction re-solved at every new geometry. `Nemo::value`
# skips the SCF when the orbitals are already converged to the requested
# threshold; that flag is dropped when the nuclei move, or the optimizer would
# walk on a frozen wavefunction (constant energy, gradients from stale orbitals).
# This case is the regression test for that: a frozen wavefunction shows up here
# as `delta-e` of exactly 0.0 across iterations and a wrong final geometry.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc --optimize --wf=nemo nemo_lih_optimize.in)

optimization
    maxiter     10
end

dft
    xc          hf
    protocol    [1e-4, 1e-6]
    dconv       1e-4
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    eprec   1e-6
    Li  0.0  0.0  0.0
    H   0.0  0.0  3.05
end
